3. METHOD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Transmit path is asserted against the WIRE, not against device 'show' output.

  Console control : pyserial on tb470, /dev/u4 @ 115200, read-only 'show' plus the
                    scoped config changes listed in section 4.
  Frame capture   : tcpdump on tb470 eth3, BPF filter 'ether proto 0x88cc',
                    -U (flush per packet), bounded by 'timeout'.
  Frame decode    : tshark -V / -T fields.
  Captures        : retained alongside this log (see section 14). Original paths on
                    tb470 were /tmp/lldp-eth3-cc.pcap, /tmp/lldp-eth3-all.pcap and
                    /tmp/lldp-neg.pcap; those are volatile and may be gone.

RATIONALE FOR WIRE-BASED ASSERTION
  'show lldp local-info' prints the device's LOCAL DATABASE — every TLV the device
  could advertise — regardless of what tlv-select actually permits on the wire.
  Asserting TLV functionality from that command alone yields a FALSE PASS on every
  optional TLV. This was demonstrated directly; see section 5.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. CONFIGURATION APPLIED TO THE DUT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Mirrors the LLDP-relevant intent of the customer config on the one port that can be
packet-captured (port1.0.23). Applied to running-config ONLY — never written to
startup-config, so a reload fully reverts the DUT.

  configure terminal
  vlan database
   vlan 72,74,76,78,255 state enable
   vlan 255 name VLAN_MGMT
   exit
  interface port1.0.23
   description to_port1.0.5_DISTRIBUTION_CCTV-02
   switchport trunk allowed vlan add 72,74,76,78,255
   lldp tlv-select all
   exit
  end

All commands accepted with no error output.
'lldp run' was already enabled globally on the DUT prior to test.

