     15:17:49.0  len  64  total_tlv=5  org127=1  nonorg=[1,2,3,0]  ttl=40

    RESULT: PASS. Every optional TLV withdrawn from the wire; frame returned to the
            50-octet mandatory-only form. The Allied Telesis proprietary TLV (127)
            persists and is NOT governed by tlv-select.

N2 — SELECTIVE ENABLE (two TLVs only, applied incrementally)
    Config   : interface port1.0.23 / lldp tlv-select port-description
                                    / lldp tlv-select system-name
    Expected : exactly and only the selected TLVs appear.
    Window   : 15:18:05.5 - 15:18:34.0   (epoch 1786331885.458 - 1786331913.961)

    show lldp interface port1.0.23
     1.0.23   Rx Tx  -- --  10.38.215.69     PdSn------ -------- -------- McNpLoPe--

    Captured frames:
     15:17:53.0  len  99  total_tlv=6  nonorg=[1,2,3,4,0]      <-- after port-description
     15:17:56.1  len 107  total_tlv=7  nonorg=[1,2,3,4,5,0]    <-- after system-name
     15:18:06.1  len 107  total_tlv=7  nonorg=[1,2,3,4,5,0]
     15:18:16.2  len 107  total_tlv=7  nonorg=[1,2,3,4,5,0]
     15:18:26.3  len 107  total_tlv=7  nonorg=[1,2,3,4,5,0]
     15:18:36.4  len 107  total_tlv=7  nonorg=[1,2,3,4,5,0]

    RESULT: PASS. Per-TLV selection is exact and incremental — TLV 4 appeared alone
            after the first command, TLV 5 joined it after the second, and no other
