11. OBSERVATIONS (not defects)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
O1  'show lldp local-info' reports the local database, not the transmitted set.
    At baseline it listed 11 optional TLVs while the wire carried none. Any test
    procedure that verifies TLV functionality from this command will pass
    incorrectly. Verify on the wire, or at minimum via 'show lldp interface',
    whose Base/802.1/802.3 bitmap did track the real transmitted set in every
    phase of this run.

O2  'lldp tlv-select all' means all NON-MED TLVs. The MED column was unchanged by
    it (McNpLoPe--, Inventory still off); MED TLVs are governed by the separate
    'lldp med-tlv-select' command.

O3  MED TLVs Mc/Np/Lo/Pe are enabled by default yet never appeared in any capture.
    This is correct LLDP-MED behaviour — a device emits MED TLVs only after
    receiving one from a MED endpoint, and tb470's eth3 is a plain Linux NIC with
    lldpd inactive. It does mean MED TLV emission was NOT exercised by this run.

O4  An Allied Telesis proprietary TLV (OUI e0:1a:ea, subtype 2, 16-octet payload)
    is transmitted in every normal LLDPDU including the mandatory-only baseline,
    is not decodable by tshark, and is not controlled by tlv-select. It is absent
    from the TTL=0 shutdown LLDPDU. Believed to be AMF-related; not confirmed.

O5  Ethernet source MAC (86:e3:27:87:09:c0) differs from the advertised Chassis ID
    (84:e3:27:87:09:c0) in the locally-administered bit. Expected AW+ per-port MAC
    derivation, but it means a device must be identified from the Chassis ID TLV,
    not from the frame source MAC.

O6  port1.0.1 (copper, 10GBASE-TM) shows 'connected' to swi_b, but no LLDP neighbour
    was learned on it — only port1.0.7 (fibre) produced a neighbour entry. Not
    investigated; most likely LLDP tx is disabled on the peer's port1.0.1. Flagged
    for follow-up, NOT pursued, as it would require configuring swi_b.

O7  tshark flags the IEEE 802.3 Link Aggregation TLV (subtype 0x03) as deprecated.
    The DUT still emits it under tlv-select all. Informational only.

