12. SCOPE NOT COVERED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
X1  MULTIPLE MANAGEMENT ADDRESSES — NOT TESTED. The customer config has two L3
    interfaces (vlan1 via DHCP, vlan255 static 10.159.8.47/23). The DUT has only
    one addressed interface (vlan1, 10.38.215.69) and emitted exactly one
    Management Address TLV. Which address AW+ selects, and whether it emits more
    than one Management Address TLV, is therefore UNVERIFIED and is a genuine open
    question for the customer's topology.

X2  STACKED CHASSIS ID — NOT TESTED. The customer runs a stack
    ('stack virtual-chassis-id 2485', stackports 1.0.27-28). Chassis ID TLV
    consistency across stack members was not verified. Deliberately not attempted:
    cabling ports 27/28 between the two tb470 IE520s puts them in a duplicate
    chassis-id / duplicate-master state with all front-panel ports err-disabled,
    and these units have no PDU, making console the only recovery path.

X3  LLDPDU SIZE CEILING — NOT REACHED. With 7 member VLANs the full LLDPDU was
    561 octets, well inside the 1500 limit. The customer's ports carry 5 allowed
    VLANs plus native, so they are in the same range. Behaviour when VLAN Name
    plus Protocol Identity TLVs would exceed one frame (many VLANs, long names)
    remains untested; LLDP has no fragmentation, so this is where truncation
    would occur if it occurs at all.

X4  LLDP-MED TLVs — NOT TESTED (see O3). No MED endpoint on the bench. The
    customer config contains no 'lldp med-tlv-select', so MED is out of scope for
    their deployment as configured.

X5  TTL EXPIRY / NEIGHBOUR AGEING — NOT TESTED.

X6  IE510-28 platform confirmation — NOT TESTED (see section 1).

